  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The material family targeted is Fe-Co-Ni-based face-centered-cubic high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The property targeted for improvement is saturation magnetization (Ms).",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The primary scientific challenge is separating the orbital magnetic moment from the spin magnetic moment.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strong crystal-field quenching impedes separation or optimization of the orbital contribution.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Complex multielement electronic hybridization impedes separation or optimization of the orbital contribution.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The total magnetic moment is represented as M = L + 2S.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fe-Co-Ni-based fcc high-entropy alloys have equimolar or near-equimolar compositions.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "These alloys exhibit high ductility.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "These alloys exhibit moderate saturation magnetization.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Their orbital moment is quenched because of cubic symmetry.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding small concentrations of Ru, Os, or Ta, or applying uniaxial strain, can break local cubic symmetry.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavy-element addition or uniaxial strain can enhance spin-orbit-coupling effects without inducing phase separation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Local symmetry breaking modifies the d-band density of states near the Fermi level.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Local symmetry breaking reduces crystal-field quenching of orbital angular momentum.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavy-element addition or strain lifts d-orbital degeneracy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lifting d-orbital degeneracy permits partial recovery of the orbital moment.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The recovered orbital moment aligns with the spin moment.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Orbital-moment recovery can increase the total magnetic moment beyond the spin-only limit if hybridization does not produce antiferromagnetic coupling.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is predicted to increase the orbital-to-spin moment ratio and saturation magnetization relative to the Fe-Co-Ni baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted magnetic improvement will occur without a significant loss of ductility.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
